Use case: precise-object-edit.
Asset type: replacement SOUTH / straight-toward-camera game animation sprite sheet, transparent PNG.
Edit target: the attached 4-column 5-row orange cat sprite sheet. Fix the orientation inconsistency in this sheet. The correct character model is the DIRECTLY FRONT-FACING cat in the BOTTOM LEFT cell, not the angled cats elsewhere.
PRIMARY REQUIREMENT: every one of the 20 drawings must have the IDENTICAL directly front-facing head, chest, shoulders, belt and hip orientation. Nose centered between the eyes; both cheeks and both shoulders equally visible. No three-quarter views, no alternating head turns, no mirrored poses. The tail remains BEHIND on SCREEN RIGHT in EVERY cell, only a gentle small tip sway; the scarf knot/ends stay on SCREEN LEFT in EVERY cell. Backpack stays behind the same shoulder. Keep all accessory sides fixed. Same head design/size, ear spacing, face/muzzle shape and clothing proportions throughout. Copy the same front head and torso model rather than redrawing a different identity each frame.
LAYOUT: EXACTLY 4 columns × 5 rows, evenly spaced cells, 20 full-body poses with generous transparent gutters. Flat alpha transparency, no colored matte, no ground/shadow, no grid/text/labels.
POSE ORDER, left to right row by row:
Cells 1–8: one coherent FRONT WALK cycle toward viewer.
1 anatomical right leg forward contact, left arm forward;
2 weight on right leg, left heel lifts;
3 left leg passes underneath body, right leg planted;
4 left leg swings forward;
5 anatomical LEFT leg forward contact, right arm forward;
6 weight on left leg, right heel lifts;
7 right leg passes underneath body, left leg planted;
8 right leg swings forward.
Cells 9–16: one coherent FRONT RUN cycle in the SAME order, with deeper knee bends, genuine airborne/passing poses, bent opposing arms. Distinct right-leading and left-leading halves, no repeated same leading boot. The head and chest still face directly at camera, no torso twist, small consistent forward lean.
Cells 17–20: front idle, inhale, brief closed-eye blink, exhale; both boots planted.
Keep the root/pelvis centered under the head and near the same height. No lateral body translation, no size changes, only natural tiny vertical bob. Both hands EMPTY throughout, sword stays SHEATHED. Orange striped cat, cream muzzle/shirt, red scarf, brown vest/backpack/belt, olive trousers, brown boots. Preserve the reference's charming softly painted anime-game art, thin clean outlines and original short large-headed proportions. This is a usable sequential animation sheet, not a collection of different perspectives. Fix the alternating body yaw and teleporting tail above all else.
